    "desc": "Everything the $ANTS page shows, composed once per request from the same cached reads. The canonical token is 0xa87EE81b2C0Bc659307ca2D9ffdC38514DD85263 (transfers gated, no market price). Net figures take the burn out: the epoch remainder is minted to the dead address, so it sits inside total_supply while held by nobody. A null is a read that failed, never a zero: a zero burn on a closed epoch is a zero read from the gate. where.slices are shares of the whole supply (minted plus rewards earned and not yet minted); the since-22 shares alone are on /ants/supply. split is the last closed epoch as the gate budgeted it, not what was paid. buy_burn.sent_to_zero_ants counts every transfer to the zero address, whoever sent it.",
    "params": [],
    "example": "/ants",
    "page": "/ants",
    "prompt": "How much $ANTS exists, how much was burned each epoch, and who holds it?",
    "cache": "live",
